1) 从告警标签取 name（卷名）与 server，确认该卷挂载在哪台主机上；:
1) Take name (the volume name) and server from the alert labels and identify which host has it mounted;
2) Log in to that host and run df -h plus du -sh /<mountpoint>/* | sort -rh | head to find the biggest consumers, cleaning up logs and temporary files first;
3) If it is still short after cleanup, expand the volume in the XSKY console and then grow the filesystem on the host (resize2fs or xfs_growfs);
4) For thin-provisioned volumes also confirm the real free space in the backing storage pool, so an overcommitted pool does not fill up for everyone at once.

1) 从告警标签取 name（桶名）与 user_name，在控制台查看该桶的对:
1) Take name (the bucket name) and user_name from the alert labels and review the object count and capacity trend for that bucket in the console;
2) Check for large numbers of historical versions or leftover multipart uploads (incomplete multipart uploads hold space indefinitely);
3) If it is still short after cleanup, raise the bucket quota;
4) Configure lifecycle rules to expire old versions automatically so this does not recur.

1) 从告警标签取 name（用户名）与 server，在 XSKY 控制台确认:
1) Take name (the user name) and server from the alert labels and confirm the quota and actual usage for that user in the XSKY console;
2) Confirm with the business owner that the growth is expected; for abnormal growth, check for duplicate uploads or uncleaned temporary objects;
3) If the growth is legitimate, raise the user quota in the console;
4) Longer term configure lifecycle rules on that user's buckets to expire old objects automatically.
